Based on my independent research, I can now issue the Round 8 verdict. All three Round 7 required fixes are verified as resolved: baseline evaluation protocol is now explicitly stated (report published numbers for competing methods, run holistic Qwen3-Coder-480B without DAG as primary internal ablation within the same mini-swe-agent harness), DebugBench has been removed, and leaderboard numbers are timestamped to 2026-05-07 with scope explicitly limited to the standardized SEAL mini-swe-agent subset. Model names (Claude Opus 4.6, GPT-5.4) are verified as real models. No new competing work found in 2026 that overlaps with the inter-hunk DAG prediction framing.

Three low-priority issues remain:

